  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $y=3$, we substitute $y=3$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(3)^{2}+(z-3)^{2} & =13 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9+(z-3)^{2} & =13 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(z-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(z-3)^{2} & ={2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $xz$-plane gives us the equation of the circle of radius $2$ centered at $(0,3).$",
